  "notes": "Acoustic-guitar-led female pop-rock: 70–118 straight with the backbeat on 2&4 and the signature singles at 90–98. Four guitar-shape majors are named (D, A, E, G) so `keys` is authored, and the harmonic colour is sus2/add9 with \"capo-driven voicings [which] mean open strings ring through changes\" — hence a high `susSubstitutionProb` and a real ninth share. Three drum deltas come from the entry: \"kick 1 and the '&' of 3\", \"8th hat with a 16th push into the chorus\" (an 8th base with the fill density lifted so the push lands), and \"tambourine layered on the backbeat from chorus 1\", which leads the perc block. The kit is \"tracked tight and mixed forward\", which is the raised accent tier against a fairly tight grid. The melody is written from \"a low-to-mid alto band, chorus a 4th above the verse, hook repeated three times per chorus\", which is the narrow register with a two-bar phrase weighting, and the \"single-note electric counter-line\" is the `answer_lick` counter. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities and `bpm.mode` 94, which is the centre of the stated signature band rather than a published figure.",
